From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:05:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 373/394] drm/msm/dpu+dsi: change the vertical front porch in
 place

A mode that differs from the running one only in the vertical front porch
(same pixel clock, horizontal timing, active height, vsync width and back
porch) no longer takes a full modeset on a DSI video-mode pipeline:
dpu_crtc_atomic_check() clears mode_changed, and at kickoff the encoder
rewrites the vertical total on the DSI hosts (and their stored mode, so the
next power-on programs it) and INTF_VSYNC_PERIOD_F0 on the INTFs, marking
them for the CTL flush -- the INTF period is double buffered and is only
latched at the next vsync after an INTF flush (without it the timing engine
keeps the old period). ACTIVE_V, the vsync position, display_v_end and the
DSC setup do not depend on the front porch.

This is how the vendor driver switches refresh rates ("DFPS": the same
DSI link, only the porch changes). A full modeset (encoder, bridge and
panel off and on) at 60 or 30 Hz makes the Lenovo TB323FU CSOT NT36523
panel flicker, while the same timings are fine when booted into or
switched in place.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
[ from github.com/joonhoekim/tb323fu-linux kernel/patches/0065 (provenance
  dbaab7f50a61bd72, 27 Sep 2026); not posted upstream ]
[mzak: adapted to the iceland queue, which already carries the hardware
 half (988f0b5c1814: vsync period of a running INTF, e6e89f3e293c: DSI
 V_TOTAL through the video timing double buffer) and the idle refresh
 worker 8165b4e0b2d8 that uses it:
 - the kickoff writes through those ops and the idle refresh write path
   (both DSI hosts and both INTFs in one section with interrupts off, not
   within 32 lines of a frame start, the INTF bits added to the commit's
   CTL flush) instead of a direct DSI_TOTAL write and an INTF op of its own;
 - both modes must run without the programmable fetch (can_set_vtotal()
   now takes the mode) instead of reprogramming it; on the OnePlus Pad 4
   VBP + VSW = 274 lines >= prog_fetch_lines_worst_case (24), so its
   120 / 60 / 30 Hz modes (pixel clock 1185840 kHz, htotal 3660, vtotal
   2700 / 5400 / 10800) never use it; 144 and 90 Hz change the horizontal
   timing and stay full modesets;
 - the check also refuses a commit that changes colour management (as
   tb323fu-linux 0079: DSPPs are only assigned in a modeset), the clone
   mode, or has an encoder that needs a modeset for its own reasons;
 - the encoder's running mode (idle refresh mode, phys cached_mode) and
   the DSI stored mode (msm_dsi_set_mode_vfp()) follow the new mode, and
   the idle rate is looked up again for it;
 - the scanout position uses the previous total for the last long frame;
 - msm.dpu_vfp_inplace (default on, read at every atomic check) turns it
   off at runtime; the encoder's debugfs status counts the changes]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
